@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] native-guest-vsock-boundary
FreeBSD and illumos guest agents MUST use Lilly's existing vsock framing and
fixed agent ports, accept requests only from host CID 2 for the current boot's
guest CID 3 binding, and refuse malformed, stale or foreign boot identities.
Agent services MUST keep credentials, terminal/workspace bytes, command
arguments and repository output out of diagnostics; closed event names and
bounded numeric outcomes are the only persistent diagnostics.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] native-agent-readiness-gate
Native services MUST bind the current boot identity before authorizing any
request. Readiness MUST additionally verify guest-local network, writable storage
and the complete live service set before returning ready. Host-only probe/trust
listeners MAY bind before SSH bootstrap so current-boot trust can authorize its
HTTPS dependencies; binding alone MUST NOT grant readiness or user authority.
A failed peer, identity or required probe MUST withhold the corresponding
ready/authorized response; stale sockets and prior-boot receipts MUST NOT grant
later service authority.
